        "original_id": "56999a5e-f734-5bd8-9105-3ce0f77e71c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Nirmul Committee\n- People: Delwar Hossain Sayeedi\n- Places: Bangladesh, East London\n- Events: Bangladesh Liberation War, protests, court sentencing\n\nFacts:\n- The Nirmul Committee was founded on 19 January 1992 by 101 Bangladeshi activists.\n- The Nirmul Committee was founded to seek justice for the genocide carried out during the Bangladesh Liberation War.\n- The London branch of the Nirmul Committee protested against the arrival of Delwar Hossain Sayeedi at a mosque in East London and demanded that his British visa be revoked.\n- In September 2014, the Supreme Court commuted Delwar Hossain Sayeedi's sentence to life imprisonment.",
